<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khunzakh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khunzakh is a village in the mountains of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on a plateau above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> Koysu river. It was the centre of the early medieval kingdom of Sarir and later the seat of the Avar khans, who ruled much of mountainous Dagestan until the Russian conquest. Its fortress was fought over during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasian-war">Caucasian War</a> of the 19th century.</p></div>
